cosmo: don't pass fds over the X transport.

cosmo's headers expose SCM_RIGHTS, so meson turns XTRANS_SEND_FDS on and the
transport's SocketRead/Writev use recvmsg/sendmsg with an SCM_RIGHTS control
buffer. On Windows that recvmsg fails with WSAEINVAL, so the server fails the
first read of every client's connection setup and drops the client. Xvfb needs
no fd passing (DRI3 is off); without it SocketRead falls back to plain
read()/writev(), which work on cosmo.

--- a/include/meson.build
+++ b/include/meson.build
@@ -192,7 +192,7 @@
 conf_data.set('LISTEN_LOCAL', get_option('listen_local'))
 
 if cc.has_header_symbol('sys/socket.h', 'SCM_RIGHTS')
-  conf_data.set('XTRANS_SEND_FDS', '1')
+  conf_data.set('XTRANS_SEND_FDS', false)
 endif
 
 if conf_data.get('HAVE_GETPEEREID').to_int() == 0 and conf_data.get('HAVE_GETPEERUCRED').to_int() == 0
